WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.810
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:06.080 --> 00:07.120
(This series is a fictional work created for entertainment purposes.)

3
00:07.200 --> 00:08.240
(The characters, events, locations, organizations agencies, as well as religions, beliefs)

4
00:08.320 --> 00:09.360
(and symbols appearing in this story are presented for storytelling purposes only.)

5
00:09.440 --> 00:10.160
(No intention is made to reference, imply, criticize)

6
00:10.240 --> 00:10.960
(or allude to any individual, organization or religious group)

7
00:12.560 --> 00:14.400
Hey

8
00:14.480 --> 00:16.520
(Chat)

9
00:20.240 --> 00:24.400
I thought I wouldn't be able to live without you

10
00:24.480 --> 00:28.160
But look at me now

11
00:28.240 --> 00:29.840
I'm shining

12
00:29.920 --> 00:31.640
On nights when the sky turns against me

13
00:31.720 --> 00:34.680
When the rain falls inside my heart

14
00:34.760 --> 00:35.720
I play the same old songs

15
00:35.800 --> 00:37.920
That we used to listen to together

16
00:38.000 --> 00:39.800
Your picture is still right there

17
00:39.880 --> 00:41.560
But I'm not crying anymore

18
00:41.640 --> 00:42.600
I used to want you so badly

19
00:42.680 --> 00:44.000
Now I'm beginning to understand

20
00:44.080 --> 00:46.920
That love comes and go

21
00:47.000 --> 00:48.880
I thought my whole world had to fall apart

22
00:48.960 --> 00:49.680
But in the end

23
00:49.760 --> 00:53.520
It was just my heart learning how to move on

24
00:54.600 --> 00:57.120
I used to say "Can't live without you"

25
00:57.200 --> 00:59.760
But today, I can proudly say, I'm cool

26
00:59.840 --> 01:00.960
I’m looking so good

27
01:01.040 --> 01:03.680
Damn I don’t even try to do

28
01:04.800 --> 01:07.240
Good without you, I’m doing fine

29
01:07.320 --> 01:09.600
Me without you, I can manage

30
01:09.680 --> 01:12.000
Already told you, don’t come back, don’t show your face

31
01:12.080 --> 01:13.960
I can still smile, easy and free

32
01:34.120 --> 01:35.240
Damn it!

33
02:06.920 --> 02:07.880
Hey!

34
02:08.479 --> 02:09.360
Hey!

35
02:10.680 --> 02:11.880
Anyone here?

36
02:38.720 --> 02:39.560
Hello.

37
02:39.640 --> 02:42.240
Chat, an insider says Ms. Nichakorn

38
02:42.320 --> 02:43.960
will be attending the meeting this morning too.

39
02:44.040 --> 02:44.920
What meeting?

40
02:45.000 --> 02:46.079
No need to ask.

41
02:46.160 --> 02:47.920
Get dressed and come out right away!

42
02:48.920 --> 02:50.120
Yeah, alright.

43
03:03.360 --> 03:04.360
Here we go.

44
03:13.880 --> 03:15.160
What to do?

45
03:16.079 --> 03:17.880
Ugh, why does everyone keep calling?

46
03:28.960 --> 03:30.480
Prepare your documents.

47
03:31.400 --> 03:32.760
He hasn’t picked up yet.

48
03:34.800 --> 03:36.360
Hello? Hello, Chat?

49
03:36.720 --> 03:38.040
Where are you?

50
03:38.120 --> 03:40.240
I'll be there in five minutes.

51
03:40.960 --> 03:43.800
Huh? Five more minutes?

52
03:44.800 --> 03:46.960
Oh no, by then Ms. Nichakorn will

53
03:47.040 --> 03:48.280
probably have arrived already.

54
03:49.320 --> 03:50.720
Please hurry up and come.

55
03:50.800 --> 03:51.880
What to do?

56
03:52.320 --> 03:54.200
The other team is here.

57
04:01.760 --> 04:02.840
Just stay still.

58
04:31.840 --> 04:33.320
Sorry! Excuse me!

59
04:35.680 --> 04:37.480
Could you help me with something?

60
04:38.440 --> 04:40.400
If Ms. Nichakorn is about to reach the elevator,

61
04:40.480 --> 04:42.080
can you please call me?

62
05:00.360 --> 05:02.680
Hello, Ms. Nichakorn.

63
05:12.880 --> 05:15.640
The target is heading straight for the elevator.

64
05:18.000 --> 05:18.960
Okay.

65
05:44.800 --> 05:46.480
What wrong with the elevator? Why is it so slow?

66
05:47.720 --> 05:48.920
Send someone to examine it.

67
05:49.000 --> 05:50.000
Yes, ma'am.

68
06:05.040 --> 06:06.200
Ms. Dao.

69
06:07.080 --> 06:08.520
Could you please go up and check

70
06:08.600 --> 06:10.360
why the elevator still hasn't come down?

71
06:10.440 --> 06:11.880
Ms. Nichakorn has been waiting for a long time.

72
06:11.960 --> 06:13.520
Oh. Umm...

73
06:13.600 --> 06:15.120
Okay. Sure.

74
06:15.760 --> 06:16.760
Thank you.

75
06:18.320 --> 06:20.280
What to do?

76
06:26.160 --> 06:28.760
Hey, brother! Go over there!

77
06:28.840 --> 06:30.120
Just go!

78
06:33.920 --> 06:35.480
I asked Dao to go check.

79
06:48.320 --> 06:49.760
Please hold on to it for a bit!

80
06:57.159 --> 06:58.280
Hey, Nueng.

81
06:59.040 --> 07:00.280
Please quickly go in, Chat.

82
07:00.720 --> 07:01.880
Did you help me?

83
07:04.400 --> 07:06.760
Please head in quickly, everyone is waiting for you.

84
07:07.200 --> 07:08.120
Mmm.

85
07:08.640 --> 07:09.880
Please wait, Chat.

86
07:26.680 --> 07:27.760
All done.

87
07:31.120 --> 07:32.040
I'll enter the room first.

88
07:32.120 --> 07:33.080
Okay.

89
07:41.240 --> 07:43.240
It's been more than five minutes.

90
07:43.320 --> 07:44.360
He's here.

91
07:44.440 --> 07:45.520
He's here.

92
07:55.480 --> 07:56.680
You made it in time!

93
07:57.480 --> 07:58.760
Almost didn't make it.

94
08:08.560 --> 08:10.520
Nueng, where did you go?

95
08:10.600 --> 08:12.160
I went to the restroom.

96
08:13.040 --> 08:15.160
I hope what you say is actually true.

97
08:16.400 --> 08:18.680
How did it go last night?

98
08:18.760 --> 08:20.600
You're the one who dates randomly.

99
08:20.680 --> 08:21.880
Geez.

100
08:21.960 --> 08:23.440
She's here.

101
08:27.040 --> 08:28.760
Hello.

102
08:28.840 --> 08:29.920
Hello.

103
08:30.000 --> 08:31.120
Please take a seat.

104
08:35.039 --> 08:36.120
Hello everyone.

105
08:36.200 --> 08:37.960
The reason I’ve called you all to an urgent meeting today

106
08:38.039 --> 08:40.799
is that I have an important announcement to make.

107
08:41.919 --> 08:43.880
It may be a major change for us,

108
08:45.080 --> 08:48.560
because a new department head will be joining

109
08:48.640 --> 08:52.400
to help oversee and support both Team A and Team B.

110
08:52.480 --> 08:55.680
He is a product specialist

111
08:55.760 --> 08:57.400
from Vega Lab Korea,

112
08:57.480 --> 09:00.080
which is already a partner of all of ours.

113
09:51.520 --> 09:54.360
Please welcome Mr. Choi Seungwoo,

114
09:54.440 --> 09:56.960
our new Head of Product.

115
10:03.960 --> 10:05.360
Hello everyone.

116
10:05.440 --> 10:06.920
I’m Choi Seungwoo.

117
10:07.920 --> 10:09.720
Nice to meet you all.

118
10:12.160 --> 10:14.760
Our product development group has two teams.

119
10:15.120 --> 10:16.320
Team A

120
10:16.400 --> 10:18.200
is led by Ms. Mira,

121
10:18.280 --> 10:20.720
with Mr. Tommy, Ms. Plai, and Mr. Nueng.

122
10:22.800 --> 10:26.760
Team B has Mr. June, Ms. Ja, Mr. Pek,

123
10:26.840 --> 10:29.120
and the team leader is Mr. Chat.

124
10:35.040 --> 10:35.880
Chat.

125
10:36.760 --> 10:37.600
Hmm?

126
10:47.440 --> 10:48.400
Hello.

127
10:52.200 --> 10:53.760
Nice to meet you all.

128
10:54.600 --> 10:55.640
I hope

129
10:56.200 --> 10:59.120
we'll work well together.

130
11:02.520 --> 11:03.840
Of course.

131
11:08.720 --> 11:10.480
I studied the work

132
11:10.560 --> 11:13.160
and products you’ve all developed carefully.

133
11:13.840 --> 11:16.480
Before we start working in earnest,

134
11:17.120 --> 11:18.840
I’d like to look at

135
11:20.280 --> 11:21.320
Team B’s work first.

136
11:33.440 --> 11:34.800
Just Team B?

137
11:34.880 --> 11:36.720
Yes, just Team B.

138
11:38.560 --> 11:39.400
Team B Leader...

139
11:41.080 --> 11:42.360
Please be prepared.

140
11:44.560 --> 11:45.400
Yes.

141
11:56.840 --> 11:58.520
Drinks are here.

142
11:58.600 --> 11:59.800
Here you go.

143
11:59.880 --> 12:00.760
Lovely.

144
12:00.840 --> 12:02.160
It’s delicious today, give it a try.

145
12:05.000 --> 12:08.400
The type of noodles little June wanted,

146
12:08.480 --> 12:10.240
here it is.

147
12:12.360 --> 12:14.280
It looks delicious!

148
12:14.720 --> 12:16.800
Oh, let me ask you something.

149
12:17.480 --> 12:19.160
People are gossiping that

150
12:19.240 --> 12:21.320
the new manager from Korea

151
12:21.640 --> 12:24.600
is handsome and totally hot. Is it true?

152
12:24.680 --> 12:27.400
Sister, true or not, just look at Tommy,

153
12:27.480 --> 12:29.000
still raving about him.

154
12:29.480 --> 12:32.960
I’ll probably have to stop loving Nueng

155
12:33.040 --> 12:35.720
and date Mr. Seungwoo instead.

156
12:36.960 --> 12:39.640
What a man, handsome like he stepped out of a drama.

157
12:40.640 --> 12:44.080
This time I’ll finally be the real female lead.

158
12:47.480 --> 12:48.760
So delusional, right?

159
12:49.160 --> 12:50.640
Last night

160
12:50.720 --> 12:52.520
I was watching a Korean drama,

161
12:52.600 --> 12:54.080
and there was this one character

162
12:54.160 --> 12:56.080
who was so delusional.

163
12:56.160 --> 12:58.480
If I could step through the screen,

164
12:58.560 --> 13:01.120
I’d yank her hair and slap them once or twice

165
13:01.200 --> 13:02.840
so they'd stop fantasizing.

166
13:06.280 --> 13:09.400
Pity the ones who want to curse but don’t dare.

167
13:09.920 --> 13:11.560
They can barely move

168
13:11.640 --> 13:13.640
because they’re on conduct probation.

169
13:13.720 --> 13:16.320
Oh, nearly getting fired too,

170
13:16.400 --> 13:19.400
so they’d better know their place.

171
13:19.480 --> 13:21.480
If you’re going to talk like that, then settle this once and for all.

172
13:21.560 --> 13:23.360
Fine, come on, come!

173
13:24.960 --> 13:26.120
Do you have some issues?

174
13:26.200 --> 13:27.080
So what?

175
13:27.560 --> 13:28.520
Huh?

176
13:28.920 --> 13:29.960
You keep taking jabs.

177
13:30.560 --> 13:32.240
If you have free time,

178
13:32.320 --> 13:34.040
go dye your hair,

179
13:34.120 --> 13:36.880
so it won’t be half black, half gray.

180
13:37.920 --> 13:39.440
But you started it, sis.

181
13:39.520 --> 13:40.920
Once doesn’t count.

182
13:44.640 --> 13:47.160
This is called fashion, dear.

183
13:47.240 --> 13:48.920
Someone with no taste like you

184
13:49.000 --> 13:51.120
has the nerve to criticize others.

185
13:51.720 --> 13:55.080
Spend your time on a hair treatment.

186
13:55.640 --> 13:57.000
All you do is spray,

187
13:57.080 --> 13:59.520
I can’t tell whether it’s your hair or your head that’s hard.

188
14:01.000 --> 14:04.680
Um, Team A and Team B usually have conflicts quite often,

189
14:04.760 --> 14:06.200
but the company views

190
14:06.280 --> 14:08.160
the problems arising from competition

191
14:08.240 --> 14:09.480
as pushing both teams

192
14:09.560 --> 14:11.880
to produce their best work.

193
14:23.360 --> 14:25.080
That’s enough!

194
14:25.440 --> 14:27.080
This is a canteen.

195
14:27.160 --> 14:28.840
If you want to fight, go fight somewhere else!

196
14:29.680 --> 14:31.160
Don’t back down, Tommy.

197
14:31.240 --> 14:32.800
If someone’s picking a fight,

198
14:32.880 --> 14:35.240
wherever it is, hit them back.

199
14:35.600 --> 14:37.440
Right, we're not selling anything anymore!

200
14:37.520 --> 14:38.640
June, don’t back down!

201
14:38.720 --> 14:39.360
Bring it on!

202
14:39.440 --> 14:40.080
Get them!

203
14:40.160 --> 14:40.760
Come then!

204
14:40.840 --> 14:42.240
Come at me!

205
14:42.320 --> 14:43.720
Enough, sis!

206
14:43.800 --> 14:45.680
Stop, stop, sis, stop!

207
14:45.760 --> 14:46.720
Every time there's a fight,

208
14:46.800 --> 14:48.400
I’m the one who ends up cleaning up!

209
14:52.040 --> 14:53.560
Enough fun.

210
15:03.560 --> 15:05.040
I think

211
15:05.120 --> 15:06.120
it’s better to give Team B

212
15:06.200 --> 15:08.880
time to prepare their presentation for the new manager.

213
15:09.800 --> 15:11.200
Your results are in the negative,

214
15:11.520 --> 15:13.480
so you’ll probably be watched closely.

215
15:17.360 --> 15:18.560
Present well,

216
15:28.280 --> 15:29.440
and be careful.

217
15:30.480 --> 15:31.960
Three months

218
15:37.920 --> 15:39.360
will become just one.

219
15:55.080 --> 15:55.920
Come on.

220
15:56.000 --> 15:57.080
Don’t buy drinks from this shop.

221
15:57.160 --> 15:58.480
It’s okay, sis.

222
16:00.960 --> 16:01.960
Chat.

223
16:09.760 --> 16:10.720
Chat.

224
16:12.600 --> 16:13.960
What's with you today?

225
16:14.040 --> 16:16.600
Why did you let team A mess with us?

226
16:19.640 --> 16:21.160
Last night I caught

227
16:21.240 --> 16:22.680
Jeno sleeping with someone.

228
16:22.760 --> 16:23.600
Huh?

229
16:24.280 --> 16:25.120
Mmm.

230
16:26.400 --> 16:28.000
So I went to a pub,

231
16:28.720 --> 16:30.000
I planned to get drunk

232
16:30.760 --> 16:32.080
but I messed up and slept with someone.

233
16:33.400 --> 16:34.640
Isn't it fine?

234
16:34.720 --> 16:36.280
Your boyfriend did it.

235
16:36.360 --> 16:37.560
So can you!

236
16:37.640 --> 16:38.520
Isn't it fabulous?

237
16:38.600 --> 16:39.760
How is it fabulous?

238
16:40.680 --> 16:42.240
The one I slept with was

239
16:44.400 --> 16:45.320
Mr. Choi Seungwoo.

240
16:46.680 --> 16:48.040
Hey!

241
16:48.120 --> 16:49.240
Mmm.

242
16:49.320 --> 16:52.080
I don't know if I should be jealous of you or pity you.

243
16:52.160 --> 16:54.120
Why does bad luck keep happening to you?

244
16:54.200 --> 16:55.520
But

245
16:55.600 --> 16:57.560
it’s a stroke of incredible good fortune.

246
16:57.640 --> 16:59.400
He's insanely handsome!

247
17:01.800 --> 17:03.920
Wait, wait, wait, wait.

248
17:05.520 --> 17:07.880
Does this mean you're on the fast track

249
17:07.960 --> 17:09.880
to having your superior as your boyfriend?

250
17:09.960 --> 17:11.680
What fast track are you talking about?

251
17:12.200 --> 17:14.119
I don't know if he remembers me.

252
17:15.000 --> 17:16.599
I hope he doesn't remember.

253
17:17.760 --> 17:19.240
What?

254
17:19.319 --> 17:20.400
Was it mind-blowing?

255
17:20.480 --> 17:21.359
Come on!

256
17:25.119 --> 17:26.319
Why is it that your team

257
17:27.000 --> 17:29.360
hasn’t had any top-form results lately?

258
17:36.120 --> 17:37.880
Can anyone answer me?

259
17:38.320 --> 17:40.440
The latest failure was my fault.

260
17:40.520 --> 17:42.280
I didn’t research the competitor’s information

261
17:42.360 --> 17:43.040
well enough beforehand.

262
17:47.760 --> 17:48.680
Umm...

263
17:49.600 --> 17:51.800
My packaging design

264
17:51.880 --> 17:53.720
also still isn’t quite up to there yet.

265
17:54.920 --> 17:57.320
I have tried to come up with the best formula possible,

266
17:57.960 --> 18:00.440
but it isn’t any different from the competitors on the market.

267
18:02.920 --> 18:04.120
What about you?

268
18:08.040 --> 18:08.880
You.

269
18:10.400 --> 18:12.480
Mr. Chat, leader of team B.

270
18:14.280 --> 18:15.120
Mr. Chat.

271
18:16.000 --> 18:17.280
Why do you think it is?

272
18:18.000 --> 18:19.880
Well, our team is about to develop...

273
18:19.960 --> 18:21.240
I didn’t ask

274
18:22.000 --> 18:23.200
what you’re working on.

275
18:23.280 --> 18:24.280
I asked why.

276
18:25.080 --> 18:26.160
Why?

277
18:34.400 --> 18:36.680
I’ll need to speak with Team B’s leader

278
18:37.280 --> 18:38.600
privately.

279
18:46.360 --> 18:47.840
Ugh, what's going on?

280
18:47.920 --> 18:49.120
It's been a while already.

281
18:49.200 --> 18:50.040
True.

282
18:50.120 --> 18:51.360
Go, go.

283
18:51.960 --> 18:53.120
Fah.

284
18:53.640 --> 18:55.560
Why is this new boss so brutal?

285
18:57.040 --> 18:58.440
I showed him around the company for quite a while,

286
18:58.520 --> 19:00.040
and he didn't seem harsh.

287
19:00.120 --> 19:01.240
I'm confused too.

288
19:01.320 --> 19:03.360
Oh, you don't know, sisters.

289
19:03.440 --> 19:05.280
When it comes to work,

290
19:05.360 --> 19:07.200
Korean people take it very seriously.

291
19:08.400 --> 19:09.640
Isn't this too serious?

292
19:10.240 --> 19:11.520
How is Chat doing?

293
19:11.600 --> 19:12.320
Yeah.

294
19:12.400 --> 19:13.920
Probably got chewed out.

295
19:18.040 --> 19:19.680
You lot watch out too.

296
19:20.200 --> 19:22.160
Be careful, or you'll be the next one to get torn to shreds.

297
19:22.240 --> 19:25.160
You team A better be careful too.

298
19:25.240 --> 19:26.680
Thanks for the warning,

299
19:26.760 --> 19:28.320
but you lot should warn yourselves instead.

300
19:28.400 --> 19:30.160
Team A is safe.

301
19:37.280 --> 19:38.120
Let's go.

302
19:39.760 --> 19:41.200
Sister, look.

303
19:52.680 --> 19:53.800
I admit it,

304
19:54.240 --> 19:56.800
Team B's performance has had some problems lately,

305
20:00.080 --> 20:02.480
but everyone is capable.

306
20:20.840 --> 20:23.360
You still can't take it out?

307
20:24.000 --> 20:25.840
Is it fun teasing me like this?

308
20:27.240 --> 20:28.320
If it was last night,

309
20:28.920 --> 20:29.960
yes.

310
20:32.240 --> 20:34.160
The sound handcuffs make when they clink together

311
20:34.840 --> 20:36.000
is pretty funny.

312
20:39.800 --> 20:41.520
Keep your jokes to yourself.

313
20:42.280 --> 20:43.240
Give me the key.

314
20:47.800 --> 20:48.600
This?

315
20:51.600 --> 20:52.480
Then

316
20:53.760 --> 20:54.840
take it back by yourself.

317
20:58.160 --> 20:59.680
Why are you doing this?

318
21:01.200 --> 21:02.560
It seems like you're having fun

319
21:03.000 --> 21:04.960
just like last night.

320
21:08.280 --> 21:09.800
Stop talking about last night.

321
21:10.240 --> 21:12.160
It will never happen again.

322
21:14.280 --> 21:15.400
And

323
21:16.480 --> 21:17.680
I’ll be waiting to see

324
21:19.240 --> 21:22.440
who it is that causes this

325
21:24.040 --> 21:24.880
to happen again.

326
21:31.600 --> 21:33.000
Here are your coffees.

327
21:37.560 --> 21:39.080
Chat already went home.

328
21:39.160 --> 21:40.480
He won't be drinking coffee with you.

329
21:44.240 --> 21:45.160
That's fine.

330
21:45.800 --> 21:47.760
I can drink two cups of coffee.

331
21:51.760 --> 21:53.560
Can you stop acting like this?

332
21:54.120 --> 21:56.320
Don't you know that what you're doing

333
21:57.000 --> 21:58.760
may get Chat in trouble.

334
22:02.720 --> 22:03.960
How does this affect you?

335
22:04.040 --> 22:06.040
The fact that you’re getting involved with Chat like this,

336
22:07.920 --> 22:09.160
if your team finds out,

337
22:10.000 --> 22:11.960
they’re definitely going to be unhappy.

338
22:12.360 --> 22:14.960
And if your team uses this to cause trouble for Chat,

339
22:16.000 --> 22:17.120
what are you going to do?

340
22:18.800 --> 22:20.440
I'm also worried about him.

341
22:20.520 --> 22:23.280
And I'll never let him get in trouble, you know?

342
22:23.920 --> 22:25.680
Your Thai tea with less sugar is ready.

343
22:33.480 --> 22:35.320
Stop looking at me in such a negative light.

344
22:41.880 --> 22:43.120
Drink something sweet

345
22:43.520 --> 22:44.760
so your mood will get better.

346
22:51.120 --> 22:52.160
I don't want it.

347
23:00.360 --> 23:01.480
You don't believe me?

348
23:09.040 --> 23:09.960
Here.

349
23:10.560 --> 23:12.360
They say sugar actually helps

350
23:12.440 --> 23:13.840
improve your mood, you know.

351
23:16.760 --> 23:17.640
Try it.

352
23:19.760 --> 23:21.040
Just a little.

353
23:34.760 --> 23:35.720
Thank you.

354
23:44.440 --> 23:46.560
(Mr. Peck)

355
24:58.520 --> 24:59.600
Teerach.

356
25:01.680 --> 25:02.520
Teerach.

357
25:02.600 --> 25:03.800
Teerach, stop.

358
25:04.960 --> 25:06.560
Your mom came up to call you,

359
25:06.640 --> 25:07.960
there must be something urgent.

360
25:08.480 --> 25:09.960
You should go see her first.

361
25:44.120 --> 25:45.120
Still not going down?

362
25:46.000 --> 25:47.320
Why do I have to go down too?

363
25:47.400 --> 25:49.200
This morning you didn’t go to congratulate

364
25:49.280 --> 25:50.640
your younger brother at the company either.

365
25:50.720 --> 25:52.040
And now you’re not going down too?

366
25:52.680 --> 25:54.120
Do I have to care about him?

367
25:56.600 --> 25:58.200
He's your younger brother.

368
26:37.320 --> 26:38.120
Hello.

369
26:39.560 --> 26:40.480
Hello.

370
26:41.320 --> 26:43.360
Hurry up and eat, so we can get this over with.

371
26:45.800 --> 26:48.520
How was your first day at work?

372
26:49.080 --> 26:50.680
Is there anything weighing on your mind?

373
26:51.680 --> 26:54.400
No. Everything is very well organized.

374
26:57.520 --> 27:00.000
No need to bring anyone else in to handle the management.

375
27:02.680 --> 27:05.200
Your brother just wanted to try working in Thailand.

376
27:08.760 --> 27:09.600
Why?

377
27:10.640 --> 27:13.240
Does your Korean father not trust you anymore?

378
27:14.160 --> 27:15.480
Is that why you're here?

379
27:17.760 --> 27:19.720
I just want some new experience.

380
27:19.800 --> 27:21.920
If you really want a new experience,

381
27:23.040 --> 27:24.840
try acting like a regular employee

382
27:25.800 --> 27:27.600
and stop telling everyone you're mom's son.

383
27:28.120 --> 27:30.120
That's the real new experience.

384
27:33.600 --> 27:35.160
I never told anyone

385
27:35.720 --> 27:36.960
that I'm our mom's son.

386
27:37.840 --> 27:38.720
Then

387
27:39.400 --> 27:40.840
please don't tell anyone, mom.

388
27:41.880 --> 27:42.880
Is that a good idea?

389
27:42.960 --> 27:44.240
That's good.

390
27:45.680 --> 27:48.320
That way we can prove once and for all whether this son of yours

391
27:49.120 --> 27:50.800
is good because of himself,

392
27:50.880 --> 27:52.080
or because of someone else.

393
28:22.000 --> 28:24.920
Why do you hate your own younger brother that much, Teerach?

394
28:33.600 --> 28:35.600
When we were kids, we had to fight over Mom.

395
28:38.400 --> 28:39.840
When he was sick,

396
28:40.440 --> 28:42.560
Mom had to go to Korea to take care of him,

397
28:44.440 --> 28:46.600
and she left me to grow up all alone here.

398
28:49.200 --> 28:50.560
When Mom came back,

399
28:54.080 --> 28:55.480
he followed her here too.

400
29:02.200 --> 29:03.920
You're acting like this

401
29:04.720 --> 29:07.240
because you're afraid of losing your mom again, right?

402
29:17.960 --> 29:19.040
Hey, doc.

403
29:19.600 --> 29:21.560
Are you analyzing the issues in my heart?

404
29:24.000 --> 29:25.440
That's not it.

405
29:27.840 --> 29:30.320
I just don't want you to drown in your own suffering.

406
29:33.440 --> 29:35.080
I'm used to living with him.

407
29:35.600 --> 29:36.800
You don't have to worry.

408
29:41.840 --> 29:44.320
I will not let everything that belongs to me be taken away.

409
30:35.360 --> 30:37.720
Why didn't you answer my calls?

410
30:41.160 --> 30:43.320
I called you all night, you know?

411
30:47.320 --> 30:48.720
I have nothing to say.

412
30:49.160 --> 30:50.840
I know I was wrong.

413
30:51.640 --> 30:53.760
I’m not going to make any excuses.

414
30:54.920 --> 30:56.520
Chat, can we...

415
30:57.560 --> 30:58.800
Let's break up.

416
31:04.080 --> 31:05.320
Are you serious?

417
31:06.720 --> 31:07.680
Mmm.

418
31:45.040 --> 31:47.200
You said you wouldn't abandon me.

419
31:53.400 --> 31:55.640
You can make me do anything for you.

420
31:59.840 --> 32:01.640
But please don't abandon me.

421
32:27.960 --> 32:29.640
It's time you grow up, Jeno.

422
32:37.200 --> 32:40.200
So, I can no longer stay here, right?

423
32:45.960 --> 32:47.400
No matter what happens,

424
32:47.480 --> 32:49.200
I would never abandon you.

425
32:51.480 --> 32:52.720
You've said it!

426
32:53.360 --> 32:54.880
If you abandoned me,

427
32:55.240 --> 32:56.880
I would have no place to go.

428
33:08.680 --> 33:10.440
Then you can stay here for now.

429
33:14.120 --> 33:15.680
The room is still vacant anyway.

430
33:18.640 --> 33:20.760
You can move out whenever you’re ready.

431
33:30.080 --> 33:31.960
This is as much as I can keep my promise.

432
34:18.920 --> 34:20.800
I'm sorry.

433
34:37.080 --> 34:39.000
Because one single mistake

434
34:39.520 --> 34:41.280
will cause everything to fall apart.

435
34:51.199 --> 34:52.239
What’s that mark?

436
34:54.320 --> 34:55.719
Let's break up.

437
34:55.800 --> 34:56.960
Chat!

438
34:57.040 --> 34:58.280
Chat!

439
34:58.360 --> 35:00.400
You said you wouldn't abandon me.

440
35:12.320 --> 35:13.480
Work-wise,

441
35:13.560 --> 35:15.160
we might be rivals,

442
35:15.480 --> 35:16.560
but

443
35:17.000 --> 35:19.080
when it comes to personal matters, I...

444
35:25.320 --> 35:26.720
I already told you...

445
35:28.840 --> 35:29.920
And I’ll be waiting to see

446
35:30.400 --> 35:33.760
who it is that causes this

447
35:34.920 --> 35:36.080
to happen again.

448
35:53.320 --> 35:55.040
How long are you going to sit there spaced out?

449
35:57.720 --> 35:59.160
So you broke up with your boyfriend,

450
35:59.240 --> 36:00.720
it’s not like the world ended, right?

451
36:04.440 --> 36:06.120
What would you understand?

452
36:08.040 --> 36:09.600
You've never been in a relationship.

453
36:10.120 --> 36:11.280
You really loved him,

454
36:12.040 --> 36:13.160
but you cheated on him,

455
36:13.600 --> 36:14.520
huh?

456
36:18.880 --> 36:20.280
I just made a mistake.

457
36:21.560 --> 36:22.920
You're my friend, okay?

458
36:23.000 --> 36:25.400
Shouldn’t you be helping me figure out how to win Chat back?

459
36:37.200 --> 36:38.600
(ROV game competition. First-place prize money 1,000,000 baht)

460
36:38.680 --> 36:39.720
See this?

461
36:40.360 --> 36:41.440
If you can win,

462
36:42.240 --> 36:44.560
he’ll be able to see that you’re taking life more seriously.

463
36:53.120 --> 36:54.720
But it's not easy.

464
36:54.800 --> 36:56.280
If you win,

465
36:57.880 --> 36:59.600
Chat will get a better boyfriend.

466
37:00.200 --> 37:02.440
But if he doesn't want you back at all,

467
37:04.280 --> 37:06.880
at least you can be proud of yourself.

468
37:11.920 --> 37:14.720
(ROV game competition. First-place prize money 1,000,000 baht)

469
37:27.960 --> 37:28.800
Hey.

470
37:30.000 --> 37:30.760
Spill the tea.

471
37:31.560 --> 37:33.440
You should’ve seen Mr. Chat’s face,

472
37:33.520 --> 37:34.600
listen.

473
37:34.680 --> 37:35.720
When Mr. Chat

474
37:35.800 --> 37:38.320
got called into the room by the Korean boss,

475
37:38.400 --> 37:39.960
you see, he came out

476
37:40.040 --> 37:42.120
looking pale as boiled chicken.

477
37:43.040 --> 37:45.040
Well, he got called one-on-one.

478
37:45.120 --> 37:46.240
He probably got scolded nonstop,

479
37:46.320 --> 37:48.040
in Thai, Korean, and English.

480
37:48.120 --> 37:50.520
Oh, if it were just a scolding that’d be fine,

481
37:50.600 --> 37:53.440
because Mr. Chat is probably used to getting scolded by now.

482
37:53.520 --> 37:55.920
But what if he gets fired?

483
37:56.000 --> 37:56.920
Oh my god!

484
37:58.800 --> 38:00.120
Like the rumors say,

485
38:00.200 --> 38:02.160
they might get fired before the three months are up.

486
38:02.240 --> 38:03.280
These days,

487
38:03.360 --> 38:04.640
if you get fired suddenly,

488
38:04.720 --> 38:05.680
how are you going to make a living?

489
38:05.760 --> 38:06.760
Well,

490
38:07.240 --> 38:09.640
there’s glazed shiny pork!

491
38:09.720 --> 38:10.720
It’s amazing.

492
38:10.800 --> 38:12.560
One bite, one liter of water.

493
38:12.640 --> 38:14.760
Sometimes when they run out of pork, they make it with dog.

494
38:14.840 --> 38:16.840
Ew, I wouldn’t dare eat it.

495
38:16.920 --> 38:17.920
I don’t even know if it’s tasty.

496
38:18.000 --> 38:18.840
It’s delicious!

497
38:18.920 --> 38:20.000
Some batches are sweet, some are sour.

498
38:20.920 --> 38:21.720
Stop joking around,

499
38:21.800 --> 38:23.160
we’re talking about something serious here.

500
38:23.240 --> 38:25.200
Honestly though,

501
38:25.560 --> 38:28.280
Team B, what are they even doing competing with Team A?

502
38:28.360 --> 38:28.840
True.

503
38:28.920 --> 38:30.040
They can’t win anyway.

504
38:30.560 --> 38:33.320
Even the team names show the class difference so clearly.

505
38:33.400 --> 38:36.040
Hey, it’d be good if Team B left.

506
38:36.120 --> 38:38.000
Fewer employees means

507
38:38.080 --> 38:39.800
the company pays out less,

508
38:39.880 --> 38:41.560
and our bonuses go up.

509
38:41.640 --> 38:44.160
Team B staying is just dead weight on the company.

510
38:51.800 --> 38:52.720
Umm...

511
38:53.680 --> 38:55.720
Would you like more water, Nueng?

512
38:56.240 --> 38:58.080
No thanks, I'm full.

513
39:10.240 --> 39:12.720
Where are the documents?

514
39:14.160 --> 39:16.040
Not this.

515
39:23.800 --> 39:25.080
Did you enter the wrong room?

516
39:25.760 --> 39:26.680
No.

517
39:26.760 --> 39:28.480
I intentionally came to see you.

518
39:29.160 --> 39:30.200
What's up?

519
39:31.680 --> 39:33.960
Well, since this morning,

520
39:34.040 --> 39:35.800
I've seen you working so hard.

521
39:36.520 --> 39:39.000
So, I wanted to ask...

522
39:39.800 --> 39:41.480
Is there anything I can help you with?

523
39:43.520 --> 39:45.560
And what would I make you help with?

524
39:49.760 --> 39:50.800
Anything is fine.

525
39:51.400 --> 39:52.920
If you need my help,

526
39:53.000 --> 39:54.160
I can do anything.

527
39:57.040 --> 39:58.760
I'm the team leader,

528
39:58.840 --> 40:00.040
I can manage by myself.

529
40:01.720 --> 40:03.200
I know you're capable.

530
40:04.720 --> 40:05.960
But if you had someone else to lend a hand...

531
40:06.040 --> 40:07.920
Your job is

532
40:08.000 --> 40:09.920
to support Team A in making their products

533
40:10.000 --> 40:10.880
the best they can be,

534
40:11.640 --> 40:14.240
since our company releases new products every single month anyway.

535
40:16.280 --> 40:17.600
As for Team B,

536
40:17.680 --> 40:20.320
we'll always be Team A's scary rival.

537
40:23.120 --> 40:24.040
Therefore,

538
40:25.800 --> 40:27.000
you’ve made a mistake.

539
40:29.080 --> 40:30.280
But...

540
40:31.680 --> 40:33.040
Thank you.

541
40:38.760 --> 40:40.280
Because you're like this,

542
40:41.080 --> 40:42.520
so I...

543
40:49.000 --> 40:50.280
Respect you.

544
40:51.120 --> 40:52.280
Mmm.

545
41:14.440 --> 41:16.480
I really admire your effort.

546
41:20.720 --> 41:21.840
Thanks

547
41:23.360 --> 41:24.600
for not getting in the way.

548
41:28.080 --> 41:29.440
It’s just not necessary.

549
41:30.480 --> 41:31.560
Because I already know that,

550
41:31.640 --> 41:33.520
Chat is never going to fall for your charms.

551
41:34.920 --> 41:35.760
Is that so?

552
41:36.440 --> 41:39.600
But usually, everyone falls for it.

553
41:43.200 --> 41:44.440
Do you think otherwise?

554
41:53.280 --> 41:54.760
Stop being so full of yourself.

555
41:55.760 --> 41:57.800
Do you think everyone is supposed to like you or something?

556
41:59.000 --> 42:01.280
It doesn't matter who likes me.

557
42:01.880 --> 42:02.960
Because I

558
42:03.600 --> 42:05.200
already have someone I like.

559
42:05.920 --> 42:07.720
It’s wrong to have feelings for someone

560
42:08.080 --> 42:09.360
who’s already taken, you know.

561
42:09.960 --> 42:11.280
Sis, spill the tea.

562
42:11.360 --> 42:12.360
Geez.

563
42:12.440 --> 42:13.840
Chat already broke up with his boyfriend.

564
42:13.920 --> 42:15.240
Huh? Already broke up?

565
42:15.320 --> 42:16.320
Break up.

566
42:16.400 --> 42:17.640
Don't go around telling others.

567
42:17.720 --> 42:18.920
Keep it to yourself.

568
42:20.600 --> 42:22.080
But it seems that this round,

569
42:23.400 --> 42:24.720
it's no longer wrong.

570
42:50.160 --> 42:51.240
Hello.

571
42:59.400 --> 43:01.000
Why did you call me here?

572
43:02.000 --> 43:03.080
Please enter first.

573
43:08.560 --> 43:09.760
I’m telling you up front,

574
43:09.840 --> 43:11.760
the only reason I came is that you said you’d unlock it for me.

575
43:12.840 --> 43:14.960
If you’re of pulling something like that again,

576
43:15.040 --> 43:16.240
I’m not playing along.

577
43:19.200 --> 43:20.040
Then

578
43:20.880 --> 43:23.120
what do you think I called you here for?

579
43:32.360 --> 43:33.720
I already told you...

580
43:38.800 --> 43:40.200
between us

581
43:40.280 --> 43:41.760
it’s only about work.

582
43:50.920 --> 43:51.840
Then

583
43:53.080 --> 43:54.680
help me look for something.

584
43:59.480 --> 44:01.320
Look for something... what?

585
44:06.360 --> 44:07.880
What kind of thing?

586
44:07.960 --> 44:09.800
I dropped my necklace here last night.

587
44:15.080 --> 44:15.960
Then

588
44:17.160 --> 44:18.760
why is the room still exactly the same?

589
44:22.720 --> 44:24.120
I called ahead and gave instructions.

590
44:26.880 --> 44:27.960
Really?

591
44:36.960 --> 44:38.880
The necklace must mean a lot to you.

592
44:44.240 --> 44:46.520
Dammit. Why didn't he say so from the start?

593
44:49.920 --> 44:51.800
What did you think I would do?

594
44:54.040 --> 44:55.080
Nothing.

595
45:20.240 --> 45:21.400
It's fine.

596
46:01.680 --> 46:02.600
If you can do every point,

597
46:02.680 --> 46:04.120
what happened yesterday won’t happen again.

598
46:04.520 --> 46:06.080
I think I have an idea,

599
46:06.160 --> 46:09.000
I guarantee Team B won’t see it coming.

600
46:09.640 --> 46:10.640
You can do it, right?

601
46:10.720 --> 46:11.800
Yes.

602
46:11.880 --> 46:13.000
If he fails,

603
46:13.560 --> 46:15.880
that means the credibility goes away with him.

604
46:15.960 --> 46:18.040
Actually, I needs to gather the information

605
46:18.120 --> 46:19.200
to bring to the meeting now.

606
46:19.280 --> 46:21.280
I need help from you.

607
46:21.360 --> 46:22.680
And if I help,

608
46:24.320 --> 46:25.160
what do I get out of it?

609
46:25.240 --> 46:26.400
You must come with me.

610
46:27.200 --> 46:28.120
Go where?

611
46:28.200 --> 46:29.160
I play the same old songs

612
46:29.240 --> 46:31.240
That we used to listen to together

613
46:31.320 --> 46:33.000
Your picture is still right there

614
46:33.080 --> 46:34.800
But I'm not crying anymore

615
46:34.880 --> 46:35.800
I used to want you so badly

616
46:35.880 --> 46:37.480
Now I'm beginning to understand

617
46:37.560 --> 46:40.240
That love comes and go

618
46:40.320 --> 46:42.240
I thought my whole world had to fall apart

619
46:42.320 --> 46:43.160
But in the end

620
46:43.240 --> 46:46.640
It was just my heart learning how to move on

621
46:47.920 --> 46:50.320
I used to say "Can't live without you"

622
46:50.400 --> 46:52.960
But today, I can proudly say, I'm cool

623
46:53.040 --> 46:54.160
I’m looking so good

624
46:54.240 --> 46:57.000
Damn I don’t even try to do

625
46:58.080 --> 47:00.440
Good without you, I’m doing fine

626
47:00.520 --> 47:02.960
Me without you, I can manage

627
47:03.040 --> 47:05.240
Already told you, don’t come back, don’t show your face

628
47:05.320 --> 47:08.040
I can still smile, easy and free

629
47:08.120 --> 47:10.440
Good without you, I’m doing fine

630
47:10.520 --> 47:12.920
Me without you, I can manage

631
47:13.000 --> 47:15.160
Already told you, don’t come back, don’t show your face

632
47:15.240 --> 47:18.320
I can still smile, easy and free

633
47:18.400 --> 47:21.120
You thought I’d cry cry cry all night

634
47:21.200 --> 47:23.600
But I’m dancing under neon lights

635
47:23.680 --> 47:26.120
Without you I’m alright

636
47:26.200 --> 47:29.600
Yeah I’m good without you, good without you

637
47:29.680 --> 47:32.120
Walking in the room now, feeling confident

638
47:32.200 --> 47:35.160
Drip Up Swag Down, Ain't got you to blem

639
47:35.240 --> 47:36.720
Now I'm Feeling loud

640
47:36.800 --> 47:39.280
All Eyes on me Now everybody Shout

641
47:39.360 --> 47:40.680
Don’t need anyone to hold my hand

642
47:40.760 --> 47:41.800
Don’t need it at all, L O V E R

643
47:41.880 --> 47:43.040
Life got better without having to fake it

644
47:43.120 --> 47:44.720
Thank you for the heartbreak. Ah

645
47:44.800 --> 47:47.400
Used to be someone who cried, but now I level up

646
47:47.480 --> 47:49.600
From a broken heart baby now I double cup

647
47:49.680 --> 47:50.880
Makeup on point, my heels so high

648
47:50.960 --> 47:52.120
See my story and you’ll have to cry

649
47:52.200 --> 47:53.040
I’m not your baby

650
47:53.120 --> 47:54.480
Glowb queen that’s my daily

651
47:54.560 --> 47:57.080
From sad girl vibe to savage mood

652
47:57.160 --> 47:59.760
Now you stuck watching me look this good

653
47:59.840 --> 48:02.040
You thought I’d be down bad

654
48:02.120 --> 48:04.520
Now I’m trending, never look sad

655
48:04.600 --> 48:06.480
You lost me? that’s your loss

656
